ouble). asref:originLongitude takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double). asref:originX takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double). asref:originY takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double). asref:sampleOffset takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double). asref:sampleScale takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double). asref:scaleX takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double). asref:scaleY takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double). asref:skewX takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double). asref:skewY takes an xsd:double or xsd:float literal (rdfs:range xsd:double)."@en .
asref:epsgCode skos:definition "The positive numeric code identifying a coordinate reference system in the EPSG registry; it is not a complete substitute for all CRS metadata."@en .
asref:gcpIdentifier skos:definition "The source-local identifier distinguishing a control point within its control-point set."@en .
asref:gcpX skos:definition "The first ground-coordinate ordinate of a control point in the declared control-point CRS."@en .
asref:gcpY skos:definition "The second ground-coordinate ordinate of a control point in the declared control-point CRS."@en .
asref:hasGeoTransform skos:definition "The complete affine transformation resource relating grid column/row coordinates to ground coordinates."@en .
asref:hasGroundControlPoint skos:definition "A measured or supplied correspondence between an image-grid location and a ground coordinate."@en .
asref:hasRationalTransform skos:definition "The rational-polynomial geolocation model associated with a resource, with its basis contract declared explicitly."@en .
asref:pixelRegistration skos:definition "Where a cell's value is located within the cell: at its centre (asref:PixelCenter, a point sample) or representing the cell from its upper-left corner (asref:PixelCorner, an area value). It describes the value, not the grid: the normalized affine (asref:GeoTransform) is always corner-based, so this property never shifts the affine or the column and row of a world point."@en .
